title: '[pallet-revive] Use an EIP-684 collision check for contract creation'
doc:
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    CREATE and CREATE2 now fail with `DuplicateContract` when the target address has a nonzero
    nonce, code, or an EIP-7702 delegation entry (active or cleared). A contract that creates
    onto such an address gets `address(0)` back. As in Ethereum, the creator's nonce is consumed
    even when the creation collides or the constructor reverts.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `ContractInfo::new` now performs the EIP-684 collision check. Out of tree callers of
    `ContractInfo::new` that install code on an existing account must switch to the new
    `ContractInfo::new_without_collision_check`. Genesis accounts with a nonce plus code and
    `eth_call` code overrides need no change.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: minor
